# Receipt-System-V3 — .gitignore
#
# The first rule below is not routine hygiene. V2 committed real financial data
# (receipt images, TINs, a live workbook) into source git history because its setup
# wizard defaulted every data path inside the program's own directory
# (`docs/apis/v3-plan-04-v2-audit-findings.md`). V3's answer is structural, not
# procedural: per-user data lives in the top-level installation directory, a sibling
# of every release clone and therefore outside this repository entirely
# (`docs/PRINCIPLES.md` §1.6, §2.4). The `config/`, `data/`, and `models/` directories
# present here are empty scaffolding that mirrors that top-level shape for local
# development — their *contents* are ignored unconditionally so a local dev run can
# never put real data somewhere `git add -A` would pick it up.

config/*
data/*
models/*
!config/.gitkeep
!data/.gitkeep
!models/.gitkeep

# Logs are rotated flat files with their own retention policy, deliberately never an
# events table and never git-tracked (`v3-plan-01-core-apis.md` #13).
#
# Anchored to the repository root deliberately. An unanchored `logs/` matches a directory
# named `logs` at *any* depth, which silently swallowed `core/logs/` — the Logs API's own
# source package — so Phase 1's scaffolding pass created 31 of the 32 Core API packages and
# nothing reported the 32nd as missing, because `git add` had simply been told to ignore it.
# The runtime log output this rule is actually for lives under the top-level installation
# directory (`docs/PRINCIPLES.md` §1.6), a sibling of every release clone, or at the repo
# root for a local dev run — never nested inside a source package.
/logs/
*.log

# Persistence's canonical store and its snapshot checkpoints — never git-tracked; the
# live SQLite file being untrackable is precisely why Historian is an in-database
# append-only table rather than a parallel git-committed event log
# (`docs/MAINTENANCE.md` §4).
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Real receipt fixtures — never committed, ever.
#
# docs/PRE_STABLE_BENCH_VALIDATION.md requires real receipt scans for every Part 1 bench
# item (synthetic substitutes are explicitly not acceptable there), and in the same breath
# requires that those scans never enter git history: a real receipt carries a real TIN, a
# real purchase history, sometimes a real name. Git history is effectively permanent and,
# on this public repo, effectively public the moment it lands.
#
# The pattern is deliberately broad rather than one exact path. The validation doc names
# `tests/fixtures/real_receipts/` as an example location ("or wherever this ends up
# living"), and a rule that only covers the one path someone happened to write down is a
# rule that fails the first time someone picks a different one.
tests/fixtures/real_receipts/
**/real_receipts/
**/real_receipt_fixtures/
tests/fixtures/**/*.heic
tests/fixtures/**/*.HEIC

# Sensitive internal documents that must never re-enter this public repository.
# LEGAL_REVIEW_NEEDED.md is a formal compliance memorandum covering real penalty exposure
# and unresolved legal risk; it was deliberately moved out of the tree in Phase 1 per
# docs/WIKI_MIGRATION_PLAN.md §3, and docs/index.md carries a stub recording that. This
# entry exists so a stray copy can never be committed by an untargeted `git add -A`.
LEGAL_REVIEW_NEEDED.md
**/LEGAL_REVIEW_NEEDED.md

# Credentials. These live in the top-level config directory, never inside a release
# clone (`v3-plan-01-core-apis.md` #27).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
service_account*.json
credentials*.json
token*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
# Per-service venvs, created inside each release clone by Setup/Update's own provisioning
# (docs/VENV_AND_IMPORTS.md §2). A generated build product of the clone, like the webapp
# bundle — and this repo is itself a clone in developer mode, so it genuinely appears here.
.venvs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# nox (noxfile.py — Forward-Compatibility Pattern validation, docs/MAINTENANCE.md) already
# self-excludes by writing its own `*`-only .gitignore inside .nox/ on first run, but that
# file doesn't exist until nox has actually run once — an explicit entry here means a fresh
# clone is protected before that ever happens, not just after.
.nox/

# Node / webapp
node_modules/
webapp/dist/
webapp/.vite/

# Release directories. Every update is a fresh clone into `<version>_<commit-hash>`,
# never a pull and never in-place mutation (`docs/MAINTENANCE.md` §2) — a clone that
# lands beside a dev checkout is not part of this repository.
x[0-9][0-9].[0-9][0-9].[0-9][0-9]_*/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
